 "summary": "Not when all candles are pooled. Across BTC, ETH and SOL, every Awesome Oscillator setting did the same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. The result that holds up is narrow: on 1h, when AO crossed down through 0 while the pair was above its 200-day SMA, the short side beat random by 0.24% after 20 candles.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long on the cross up through 0",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, pooled and on each of BTC, ETH and SOL."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the cross down through 0",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random when all candles are pooled, on 1h, 4h and daily. The one exception is 1h in uptrends, where the short side beat random by 0.24% after 20 candles."
  },
  {
   "use": "Trading the side of zero (above or below 0)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Holding long above 0 or short below 0 was the same as random on 1h, 4h and daily."
  },
  {
   "use": "Going long on the turn up below 0 (crosses up its 5-bar SMA)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random pooled on every timeframe. On daily in uptrends it did worse than random by 7.48% after 20 days."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, AO crossing up through 0 gave 3,626 entries in 2,761 separate moves. After 20 candles they matched random entries, at 0%. The same cross on 4h landed in the same place, and on 1h uptrends and downtrends were both the same as random. On daily in downtrends it beat random by 4.35%, but that rests on one signal on Jan 6, 2023.",
  "Shorting AO's cross down through 0 on 1h was the same as random when pooled, at 0.07%. Split by trend, the picture changes. With the pair above its 200-day SMA, the short side beat random by 0.24% across 1,982 entries. It shows at 10 and 20 candles, fades at 50 and 100, and holds without its strongest stretch of May 18–19, 2021. Below the 200-day SMA the same cross showed nothing.",
  "Single stretches can fake a result. On 1h, the ETH short on the cross down through 0 looked better than random only because of signals on May 10–11, 2022, during the Terra collapse. On 4h, the SOL long above 0 rests on the run between Jul 21 and Sep 12, 2021. Without that run it is the same as random.",
  "Holding a position on the side of zero fires on almost every candle. On 1h, long above 0 gave 82,840 entries but only 1,634 separate moves, inside the luck band. On daily in uptrends, the short below 0 beat random by 6.48% after 20 days and holds without its strongest stretch. It rests on only 43 moves and fades at 50 and 100 days. The daily long above 0 in uptrends was fragile, resting on the run between Aug 1 and Nov 19, 2021.",
  "AO crossing up its 5-bar SMA below 0 gave 6,061 entries on 1h and matched random. On daily in uptrends it did worse than random by 7.48%, also at 10 days, and holds without its strongest stretch. In downtrends on daily it beat random by 2.94%, but only because of signals between Jun 17 and Jun 29, 2023. A bot needs two conditions for this setting: the SMA cross and AO below 0.",
  "For a long DCA bot, the AO zero cross adds nothing to entry timing on these pairs, so the DCA orders and take profit do the work. The 1h cross down through 0 in uptrends is a filter, not a trigger: 0.24% after 20 candles is smaller than most take profits. You could use it to pause new long deals for a few candles after it fires while the pair sits above its 200-day SMA. In downtrends it showed nothing, so leave it out there."
 ],
